    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0509" n="499" xml:id="pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00 Manchuria/8–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-19T16:00:00+03:00">August 19, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 20—3 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2092. French Ambassador here states French Embassy Nanking reports that during
                    June relations between military forces Manchuria and those North China became so
                    acute that Mao and Manchurian commander appealed to Moscow to arrange <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>. In response that appeal one
                    Sokolikov despatched from Moscow and arranged an agreement substantially as
                    follows: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Manchurian troops would not move south, and North China troops would
                            not move north of the Great Wall without specific mutual
                            agreement.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>At time of establishment of Central Chinese Communist Government, in
                            consideration of special position of Northeast China a special agreement
                            on relations between Manchuria and central authorities will be worked
                            out.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>This Embassy has no information re Sokolikov. Please protect source this
                    report.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated Nanking 89.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
